From 7061051704dcc5bbc5ff630ead4914edf1ace8ae Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Thiago Duarte <me@tduarte.co>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 17:43:09 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] libcamera: software_isp: Add contrast autofocus

Port of the fp6-img libcamera 0.7.2 autofocus series to the 0.8.0 softisp
IPA (src/ipa/simple was renamed to src/ipa/softisp and rebuilt on libipa,
so the original patches no longer apply):

  libcamera: software_isp: Add focus control (Vasiliy Doylov)
  libcamera: software_isp: Add autofocus (Vasiliy Doylov)
  AF: detect focus loss (Vasiliy Doylov)
  af: two-phase sweep over a brightness-normalised centre window (Pavel Machek)
  libcamera: pipeline: simple: Apply the lens position unconditionally
  libcamera: software_isp: af: Harden the lens control handling
  libcamera: software_isp: af: Add AfMode and focus without a trigger
  libcamera: software_isp: af: Re-baseline the scene reference after a sweep
  (Jorijn van der Graaf)

The algorithm (af.cpp) is unchanged. What changed is the plumbing: the
sharpness statistic is added to the 0.8.0 SwIspStats accumulation macros
(including the quad-Bayer path), the lens ControlInfoMap travels in
ipa::softisp::IPAConfigInfo, and setSensorControls carries a second
ControlList for the lens. The frame context gains a lens.valid flag so the
lens is only written when the Af algorithm ran.

Compile-tested only at this commit.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
